From 309bbce5030e9ed8c0427c7a42d9b7e488f1538d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:43:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] SX1262/SX1261/SX1268 LoRa radios with a shared air

The SX126x command interface on SPI: run on NSS rising, the status
byte shifted out during opcodes and status positions, BUSY while a
command runs (calibration 3.5 ms, cold start, sleep until NSS falls),
NRESET, DIO1 from the IRQ masks. Standby/sleep/FS/TX/RX (single,
timed, continuous, duty cycle)/CAD, packet type, frequency,
modulation and packet parameters, buffers and base addresses,
registers (version string, sync word, random numbers), IRQ, RX buffer
and packet status, instantaneous RSSI, errors and stats.

TX_DONE comes after Semtech's LoRa time on air for the parameters.
With chardev=, packets go to and come from other radios (another QEMU,
or many through a hub that sets RSSI/SNR, loss and corruption): a
radio listening on the same frequency, SF, BW, sync word and IQ gets
the packet at its end (RX_DONE, HEADER_VALID, CRC_ERR if corrupted);
overlapping packets collide unless one is 6 dB stronger; CAD and
GetRssiInst see the channel busy.
